gcm/live-draw: every live host target and every path between them ready for an internal scale, and native-size guards
at every guest-visible boundary; the scale stays 1x.

Purpose (issue #55, step 2 of the internal resolution scale): the fixed-2x path needs every host resource that
live-draw renders into or copies between to be held at one scale, and the game must only ever see its own resolution
(the maintainer's condition). This patch makes every such path take the scale and adds the guards; the scale itself
stays native, so nothing changes at 1x. Patch 6082 sets it from RSX_INTERNAL_SCALE (it applies after the FSR 1 and
present patches it has to touch). ENHANCEMENT: the PS3 renders at its own resolution only.

Change (all in libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c unless named):
- Allocation at the physical extent (guest sample size times the scale): colour surfaces (surface_get), zetas and
  their depth snapshots (zdepth_get, zdepth_grow_snapshot; snapshot_w/h stay the guest size for 2021's unnormalised
  divisor and 2063's windows, snap_pw/ph is the physical size), the shared depth, the 2063 zeta windows, the 2087/2097
  surface windows, the 2065 R16G16 copy, and the 2023 FXAA and 2070 gamma targets. The feedback copy is made from the
  surface's own description. ld_iscale_activate() runs once at start, before the shared depth is made.
- Copies and passes between them scale their boxes, origins and dispatch sizes: the surface and zeta windows, the 1:1
  resolve copy and ld_downsample (the k x k box stays k x k), ld_scaled_blit's destination rect (its source rect is
  normalised), the NV3089 GPU blit, the depth snapshot and R16G16 dispatches. Draw viewport, scissor and clear rects
  were already mapped by 2300.
- The game's boundary (ld_is_down / ld_is_up_rows / ld_is_count): a scaled surface gets a companion at its guest size
  (same format, RENDER_TARGET, made on first need, replaced with the surface; one SRV and one RTV per surface slot).
  Before a write-back (ld_rb_record, the batched path; rsx_live_draw_debug_read_surface, the per-surface path and the
  host tests' hook) and the movie-caption capture, one pass refreshes the companion from the surface and the existing
  copy reads the companion: R8G8B8A8_UNORM and R16G16B16A16_FLOAT average the scale x scale texels, R32_FLOAT takes the
  top-left one, so data is never blended. Guest rows uploaded into a scaled surface (ld_gv_upload_rows, used by 2017's
  validation and 6008's SPU puts) land in the companion and are expanded nearest-neighbour. Occlusion counts written to
  the guest (2027) are divided by the texels per guest sample, rounded up (rsx_internal_scale.h
  rsx_iscale_count_to_guest): 0 stays 0, any coverage counts at least 1. CPU depth probes read the first physical
  texel of their guest point. ASSUMPTION: an RGBA8 or FP16 surface that reaches the guest holds colour.
- Shaders: WPOS (2088) and DDX/DDY (2096) divide by the AA grid composed with the scale (ld_wpos_divisor). On a scaled
  target WPOS keeps each texel's sub-pixel position, pixel + (j + 0.5) / scale, so screen-space lookups into a scaled
  G-buffer stay texel-exact; the 1x text is unchanged. ASSUMPTION: no guest program needs WPOS to be exactly the pixel
  centre (floor(WPOS) is unchanged). ld_xl_in carries the scale (0 at 1x) and the pipeline key hashes it only when it
  is not 0, so 1x keys, warm caches and PSO template records are unchanged; template records are written at 1x only
  and prewarmed with the live scale after their 1x key is checked.
- Diagnostics: LD_SURF_DUMP / LD_FRAME_DUMP and the zeta PFM dump write the host image (physical size).

At 1x every ld_isx/ld_isy is the identity, every allocation, box, dispatch, key and shader text is as before, and no
companion is made (ld_is_down returns the surface itself).

Verification: tools/runtime/test_internal_scale_map.sh (with 6082). rsx_live_draw.c compiled with MinGW-w64 gcc 16.2 at
-O2 -Wall -Wextra with no new diagnostics. A native Windows 11 build of the series ran at 1x and at 2x (see 6082).

Written for this port; not taken from RPCS3 or any other emulator.

--- a/libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h	2026-11-13 15:36:29.082940100 -0800
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_internal_scale.h	2026-11-13 16:16:58.342004600 -0800
